  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the canyon scene. It passes `typecheck`, but I could not run `vite build` or open the page, so I have not seen a rendered frame. The colours, fog density and shadow settings are untuned guesses.\n\n- **Canyon:** one custom heightfield mesh, about 30k vertices, built in code with no external assets. A winding canyon with a riverbed channel is cut into stepped sandstone walls. The walls have flat ledges, cliff faces and vertex-colour strata in red, orange and sand.\n- **Props:** instanced boulders, angular rock slabs and dead shrubs made from thin branch cylinders.\n- **Sky and light:** a gradient sky from violet-blue at the top to magenta and orange near the horizon. The sun is an orange directional light at 11° elevation with cascaded shadows. A hemisphere light and a faint cool fill light brighten the shadowed sides. A warm mauve exponential fog (density 0.0075) fades distant walls toward the horizon colour, and a light bloom is added.\n- **Camera:** a 53-second loop at 3 m/s along the canyon floor at about 1.8 m eye height. It drifts left and right and looks slightly upward. The canyon repeats every 160 m, so the loop has no visible jump at the wrap, which assumes the fog hides the far end of the mesh.\n- **Contract:** the app draws into the existing `#app` canvas with `resize: false`, and `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames. I avoided the look presets because they load HDRI files that `public/` does not contain, and those requests would log console errors.",
